{"id":"00000001794401823450:d69c66adc93da63360e3ecfe1534c0a3","text":"Review of PR #1189 at 0243ff40ca52885d532b2cf5e44f6f8bb38ee148: approve. No blocking findings; no edits or pushes.\n\nTESTED: bun run test -- src/router/getRoutes in packages/one through normal narrow admission: 1 file passed, 3 tests passed. Validation score: launch 8/10, functionality 8/10. No @vxrn/color-scheme build problem occurred.\n\nTESTED: a disposable bun -e probe using the real globbedRoutesToRouteContext and getRoutes with ignoreEntryPoints true suspended first on root, then on an unvisited sibling layout, and returned initialRouteName index on the third attempt. Neither leaf page importer ran. This establishes actual client-context compatibility, beyond the synchronous mock in the added test. A second bounded development probe with two sibling layout importers delayed 550 ms completed with started=[root,a,b]. The suspected eviction/restart loop did not occur: resolve clears each visited module eviction timer. Probe scores: launch 9/10, functionality 8/10. These probes exercised route initialization directly, not a rendered native deep link or browser hydration.\n\nINFERRED from getRoutes.ts:828-898 and the runtime observations: the crawl is client-compatible and performs no filesystem access, context.resolve, server entry lookup, API import, or leaf screen load. It loads every layout through the existing loadRoute boundary, validates initialRouteName, applies group overrides, sets initialRouteName, and traverses children. It does not traverse slots, a pre-existing limitation unaffected here. No other crawl branch depends on ignoreEntryPoints. With entry points enabled, previous behavior is preserved; with them disabled, the arrays remain undefined. Ancestor entry-point arrays are still constructed locally but have no additional externally visible effect. No simplification or DRY merge is required for this narrow fix.\n\nINFERRED cost/side effects: not free. Previously deferred layout modules, their transitive imports and top-level effects now execute during initialization, including layouts outside the requested route. The real context throws pending promises, so cold layout loads proceed serially with traversal restarted after each suspension. The router caches the completed tree for a stable context, so this is initialization/HMR cost rather than per-navigation work. No timing benchmark was performed. This cost is the existing settings-discovery design and is necessary to read runtime layout exports with this approach.\n\nINFERRED web behavior: changed too, because router.ts:277 uses the same getRoutes options for native, web client, and runtime SSR. Web now honors exported initialRouteName/group overrides in linking configuration and screen sorting, validates invalid settings, and eagerly loads previously unvisited layouts. It is not a native-only change. Client and runtime SSR use the same discovery path; server manifest calls already ran this crawl. The existing getReactNavigationConfig comment explicitly documents eager layout loading as a known settings-discovery cost.\n\nThe claim is supported: the skipped crawl was the active reader of unstable_settings and the change restores initial route metadata without assigning entryPoints on the client.\n\nREVIEW: approve"}
